# Background task b9e02a2951c926b2f — output will appear here
commit e8a66ea9fe2cdb0d21265e646a533a69247b72cd
Author: TimeMagic <chenzijian@bupt.edu.cn>
Date:   Wed Apr 29 01:08:28 2026 +0800

    feat(338): Kernel Message SSE — submit/observe split architecture
    
    - POST /v1/sessions/{id}/messages returns JSON RPC handle {run_id, anchor_sequence, injected, status}
    - GET /v1/sessions/{id}/stream is session-scoped persistent SSE with Last-Event-ID resume
    - Delete old sync message endpoint, old long-poll /events, and SendMessageRequest.stream
    - Add RunOrigin enum (user/background_task/heartbeat) wired through runs registry and run_status events
    - Add ToolPresentation layer with visible/label/summary/detail contract
    - Rewrite realtime_stream hook to emit assistant_message, tool_start, tool_end, run_status
    - ServerClient: submit_message() + stream_session() with _IncrementalSseParser
    - CLI REPL: persistent SessionStreamReader background thread, per-turn SSE drain
    - CLI --text: NDJSON output filtered by run_id until terminal run_status
    - Gateway inbound pipeline: submit + stream_session consumption with fallback path
    - Origin header rendering for non-user runs in CLI and Gateway outbound routing
    - Run Activity mapping helper ready for feat-336 consumption
    
    Milestones: M1 Hub Extensions → M2 RunOrigin → M3 Presentation → M4 Realtime Hook →
    M5 Endpoints → M6 Client Streaming → M7 CLI Wiring → M8 Gateway Cutover → M9 Cleanup
    
    Acceptance: A1–A10 verified via unit/integration tests and CLI help smoke test.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

